singleadcjoy: take placeholder key codes from the device tree.

The driver unconditionally advertised BTN_THUMBR so a board without a
right-stick click still got the button indexes of the RGB20Pro's layout, which
is what dArkOS's SDL mappings expect. SDL numbers buttons by the advertised key
codes, so that phantom code shifts every later index on any board targeting a
different layout: with the GO-Super Gamepad layout AmberELEC's configs use, it
lands between R2 and the D-pad and moves the D-pad, select and start by one.

Read the codes to advertise from an optional "linux,placeholder-codes" property
instead. Boards that need none get none; a board missing a button of its target
layout lists that button's code.

--- a/drivers/input/joystick/singleadcjoy.c	2026-09-27 19:26:20.132757358 +0200
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/singleadcjoy.c	2026-09-27 19:26:20.152759058 +0200
@@ -1163,21 +1163,24 @@
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * dArkOS/RGB20Pro SDL mapping compatibility:
-	 *
-	 * RGB20Pro advertises BTN_THUMBR even when Miniloong may not have
-	 * a physical right-stick click. SDL enumerates joystick buttons from
-	 * the advertised evdev key capabilities. Without BTN_THUMBR, Miniloong
-	 * maps:
-	 *   dpup:b12, dpdown:b13, dpleft:b14, dpright:b15
-	 *
-	 * RGB20Pro maps:
-	 *   rightstick:b12, dpup:b13, dpdown:b14, dpleft:b15, dpright:b16
-	 *
-	 * Advertise BTN_THUMBR so the button indexes match RGB20Pro.
-	 * No event is generated unless a DTS GPIO also reports BTN_THUMBR.
+	 * SDL numbers joystick buttons by the key codes a device advertises, so a
+	 * board missing a button its target layout has (e.g. no right-stick click)
+	 * shifts every later index. "linux,placeholder-codes" advertises such codes
+	 * without a GPIO behind them - no event is ever reported for them - so the
+	 * indexes match the layout the board's configs were written for.
 	 */
-	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, BTN_THUMBR);
+	{
+		int i, count = device_property_count_u32(dev, "linux,placeholder-codes");
+
+		if (count > 0) {
+			u32 *codes = devm_kcalloc(dev, count, sizeof(*codes), GFP_KERNEL);
+
+			if (codes && !device_property_read_u32_array(dev,
+					"linux,placeholder-codes", codes, count))
+				for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+					input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, codes[i]);
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (joypad->auto_repeat)
 		__set_bit(EV_REP, input->evbit);
